{"statement_verdicts":[{"obj_id":"thm:main","verdict":"matched","note":"The Lean statement is equivalent to the paper's, read modulo the source-attested cited carrier CompanionMomentSaving (prop:companion). Tree: BoundedTree B is a prefix-closed set of words over Fin B, which caps branching at B. MainTree requires infinitude and 0<B, and 0<B already follows from infinitude. Every rooted tree with at most B<∞ children per vertex is isomorphic to such a set of words, so the paper's class of trees is captured. lambda: MainLambda is 0<lam<1, as ass:main-lambda states. a_infinity: limitInfo is limUnder of levelInfo, and levelInfo n = Σ_obs P(obs)·TV(posterior of the root given the level-n spins, uniform). The TV is ½Σ|p_i−1/4| and comes from broadcastJoint, i.e. a uniform root and independent edge channels as in eq:channel. Because the sequence decreases and is bounded, limUnder is the actual limit. The uniform fallback posterior on null observations carries zero weight. Capacity: capacity3 is the ENNReal supremum of ofReal|θ| over nonnegative flows. Each flow is indexed by the child endpoint of its edge, vanishes off T, and conserves mass at every nonroot vertex (so it is zero at leaves). Admissible flows satisfy V_λ ≤ 1 on every ray of ∂T, where V_λ = Σ_e (λ^{-2|e|}θ(e))^2 and |e| is the depth of the child endpoint (n+1). This matches def:flow, def:edge-boundary and def:capacity. The supremum is never empty, because the zero flow is admissible, and 0<sup in [0,∞] matches the paper. Extra hypotheses: EuclideanNormPin and ProductRulePin restate the pinned readings ass:pin-1 and ass:pin-2. Both are provable, so they add no restriction and do not make the statement vacuous. EuclideanNormPin is the standard Euclidean norm identity. ProductRulePin holds because withDensity Z of mu⊗nu puts full mass on simplex×simplex∩{Z>0}, where every admissible extension equals productP, so the image measures coincide. Optional cleanup: discharge both pins as lemmas instead of keeping them